7592186311588 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186310976 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311588 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311181 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311588 #edb/ref 1069 "q-335424" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311588 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311588 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the inhomogeneous system  ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x({t}_{0})$ is presented below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $y(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $y(t)-y({t}_{0})={\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $y({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0})$ \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $y(t)=x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$  \n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)=x(t)$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ by  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L8}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-3}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311588 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8d22d3f6-665f-591f-8d24-fd114ca419a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311588 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Integrating ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t)$ from ${t}_{0}$ to $t$ in $\\text{L3}$ yields\n\n$$\ny(t)-y({t}_{0})={\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ by $\\text{integrating both sides from }{t}_{0}\\text{ to }t.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L5}.$ Evaluating $y(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)$ at $t={t}_{0}$ gives\n\n$$\ny({t}_{0})={e}^{-A({t}_{0}-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})=Ix({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{evaluating at }t={t}_{0}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L8}.$ Multiplying both sides of\n\n$$\ny(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L1}$ by ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t) & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t) \\\\  & =x(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L8}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{multiplying both sides by }{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311589 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186310863 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311589 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186310906 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311589 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311029 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311589 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311107 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311589 #edb/ref 1069 "q-335425" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311589 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311589 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the inhomogeneous system  ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x({t}_{0})$ is presented below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $y(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $y(t)-y({t}_{0})={\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $y({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0})$ \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $y(t)=x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$  \n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)=x(t)$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line\n{{field-2}}\nby substituting \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L9}$ follows from line $\\text{L7}$ by  \n{{field-4}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311589 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "422e58f9-3604-570b-8c52-db745e03b518" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311589 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Differentiating $y(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)$ and applying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =({e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})})^{′}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(-A){e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{differentiating and using the product rule}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L4}$, $\\text{L5}$, and $\\text{L6}.$ From $\\text{L4}$ we have\n\n$$\ny(t)-y({t}_{0})={\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nUsing $y({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0})$ from $\\text{L5}$, this becomes\n\n$$\ny(t)-x({t}_{0})={\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nso\n\n$$\ny(t)=x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L4}$ by substituting $y({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0}).$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L7}$, $\\text{L8}$, and $\\text{L9}.$ From $\\text{L8}$ we know that\n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)=x(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)=x(t)$ into\n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L7}$ gives\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L9}$ follows from $\\text{L7}$ by $\\text{substituting }{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)=x(t).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370307 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370308 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370307 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370309 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370307 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370310 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370307 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370311 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370307 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370307 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370307 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186370310 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370307 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "04307a93-eb46-548d-9a4a-4bf90a0e6697" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370308 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)+1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370308 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370308 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "01b710ba-ff00-564b-aa56-a218823c5a34" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370309 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370309 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370309 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "115a425c-7d5a-5e6a-a6a9-f0d774f944ae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370310 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370310 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370310 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "039d6594-16e9-5ee1-a93f-756747ec02c2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370311 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)+1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370311 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370311 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e2c3a851-f331-52ed-aa7f-b2a15aaca90c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396516 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186396517 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396516 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186396522 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396516 #edb/ref 1069 "q-334924" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396516 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396516 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x(1)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"170px\">$3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-1))+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-1))$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td><td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"170px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td><td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">${e}^{2s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s))$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396516 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e1bc76f0-5438-50ce-a2c1-3d7bf5ef80b4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396516 #edb/ref 1074 "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-1)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-1)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-1)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-1))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-1))+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-1)) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-1))+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-1))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2s} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ {e}^{2s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-1))+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-1)) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-1))+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-1))\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{1}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ {e}^{2s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396517 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396518 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396517 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396519 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396517 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396520 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396517 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396521 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396517 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396517 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396517 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186396519 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396517 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "03a43476-4b63-5b9c-a60e-49518b095eb0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396518 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{2s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s))" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396518 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396518 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "724c6608-ba55-593a-b831-9342a1ad2fe4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396519 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{2s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s))" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396519 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396519 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6d012455-60c7-55cd-8abe-a5ae87c14843" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396520 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{2s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t+s))" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396520 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396520 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f37ded06-8f51-502f-9066-f2e3021a9d5c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396521 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{2s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t+s))" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396521 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396521 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "61927b3b-fbb4-54e5-bcfd-ea2b2a79e95e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396522 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396523 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396522 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396524 #edb/re